{#- One mixed timeline: the rows of a view page (/t/, /r/, /log/) and of a
    group's landing page. Callers set `entries`; each is a fragment (subject,
    face, html, url) or an essay (title, blurb, url). Pulled out of view.njk
    on 2026-11-03 so the group page's log is the same rows. A fragment that
    wore a face (`## Bears` under NFL) shows the face's name and cover. -#}
    {% for entry in entries %}
    {#- The art repeats here because this is the one timeline that MIXES
        subjects: the cover says which game before the label has been read.
        An essay is its own thing, not a subject — its row carries its title
        over a blank art column (the daily's FRAG_LOOSE, which keeps loose
        prose in line with its neighbours), and its lede links to its /e/
        page, the full text's one home. Rating views carry no essays at all
        (an essay is about a game, not a verdict on one), so this branch
        simply never fires there — no conditional needed. -#}
    {% if entry.kind == "essay" %}
    <div class="frag">
      <span class="sky sky-blank" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="frag-body">
        <a class="essay-title" href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.title }}</a>
        <a class="fragment-date" href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.date | readableDate }}</a>
        <p class="tag-essay">{{ entry.blurb }}</p>
        <a class="more" href="{{ entry.url }}">read →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% else %}
    {%- set box = entry.face.box if entry.face else entry.subject.coverBox %}
    <div class="frag"{% if box %} style="--box:{{ box }}"{% endif %}>
      {{ entry.subject.slug | subjectSky(entry.face) | safe }}
      <div class="frag-body">
        <p class="fragment-meta">
          <a class="fragment-date" href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.date | readableDate }}</a>
          <a class="fragment-subject" href="/s/{{ entry.subject.slug }}/">{{ entry.face.title if entry.face else entry.subject.title }}</a>
        </p>
        {{ entry.html | safe }}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
